# `actuarial::endowment_insurance`

Expected present value of an endowment insurance of 1.

## Signature

```cpp
pluss::Series actuarial::endowment_insurance(const pluss::Series &qx, double interest_rate);
```

## What It Does

Returns {math}`A_{x:\overline{n}\vert}=A^1_{x:\overline{n}\vert}+{}_nE_x`: 1 at the end of the year of death if death occurs within `n` years, or 1 at the end of the term if the life survives, so the benefit is certain to be paid and only its timing is uncertain. It is [`cashflow::endowment`](../valuation/endowment.md) on a flat rate. At a zero rate it is exactly 1; at a positive rate it is below 1 by the discounting of the later payments.

## Parameters

`qx`
: One-dimensional, finite series of one-year death probabilities in {math}`[0,1]`; the horizon is its length.

`interest_rate`
: The annual effective rate {math}`i`, finite and greater than −1. A zero or negative rate is valid.

## Returns

A rank-zero series: the expected present value of a benefit of 1 per unit, read with `item<double>()`.

## Errors

Throws `survival_curve: qx must be defined`, `survival_curve: qx must be 1D`, `survival_curve: qx must be finite` and `survival_curve: qx values must lie in [0, 1]`, and `discount::flat: rate must be finite` and `discount::flat: rate must be > -1`.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1: five years at 4%

The cost of a certain payment of 1 whose date depends on death.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const pluss::Series qx = pluss::make_series({0.010, 0.012, 0.015, 0.019, 0.024});
  out.writeln(actuarial::endowment_insurance(qx, 0.04).item<double>());
}
```

### Example 2: by hand

The term insurance plus the pure endowment.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(8));
  const pluss::Series qx = pluss::make_series({0.010, 0.012, 0.015, 0.019, 0.024});
  out.writeln(actuarial::term_insurance(qx, 0.04).item<double>() + actuarial::pure_endowment(qx, 0.04).item<double>(), actuarial::endowment_insurance(qx, 0.04).item<double>());
}
```

### Example 3: no interest

A certain benefit of 1 is worth 1 undiscounted.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(8));
  const pluss::Series qx = pluss::make_series({0.010, 0.012, 0.015, 0.019, 0.024});
  out.writeln(actuarial::endowment_insurance(qx, 0.0).item<double>());
}
```

### Example 4: the discount only

With no mortality it is the discount factor to the end of the term.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(8));
  out.writeln(actuarial::endowment_insurance(pluss::make_series({0.0, 0.0, 0.0}), 0.05).item<double>(), std::pow(1.05, -3.0));
}
```

### Example 5: the effect of the interest rate

A higher rate lowers the value of money paid in the future.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const pluss::Series qx = pluss::make_series({0.010, 0.012, 0.015, 0.019, 0.024});
  for (const double i : {0.0, 0.02, 0.04, 0.08})
    out.writeln("i =", i, " value =", actuarial::endowment_insurance(qx, i).item<double>());
}
```

### Example 6: the effect of the horizon

Each added year of mortality extends the benefit.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const pluss::Series full = pluss::make_series({0.010, 0.012, 0.015, 0.019, 0.024, 0.030, 0.037});
  for (const int n : {2, 4, 7})
    out.writeln("n =", n, " value =", actuarial::endowment_insurance(full.slice(0, 0, n, 1), 0.04).item<double>());
}
```

### Example 7: the errors

Invalid probabilities and interest rates are refused.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const auto report = [&](const auto &call) {
    try {
      call();
    } catch (const std::exception &e) {
      std::string text(e.what());
      if (const auto cut = text.find("Triggered"); cut != std::string::npos) text.erase(cut);
      while (!text.empty() && text.back() == '\n') text.pop_back();
      out.writeln(text);
    }
  };
  report([&] { (void)actuarial::endowment_insurance(pluss::make_series({0.1, 1.5}), 0.04); });
  report([&] { (void)actuarial::endowment_insurance(pluss::make_series({0.1, 0.2}), -1.0); });
  report([&] { (void)actuarial::endowment_insurance(pluss::make_series({0.1, 0.2}), std::nan("")); });
  report([&] { (void)actuarial::endowment_insurance(pluss::make_series({0.1, 0.2}).reshape({1, 2}), 0.04); });
}
```

